 "Solutions, votes and reactions": "help:using-the-community",
 "Some players have told us VoiceOver can lose its place while swiping through a board. We have found the cause: a card offering help can open on its own while you are reading the board. A fix is on its way in an update. Until then:": "help:troubleshooting",
 "Something I bought did not arrive": "help:troubleshooting",
 "Starting a thread and replying": "help:using-the-community",
 "Still missing? Write to us privately with the [contact form](/contact), with the date and the item. Never post a receipt in the community. Refunds are handled by Apple: see [Refunds](/refunds).": "help:troubleshooting",
 "Tap **Post thread**. To reply, use the box at the foot of a thread, or **Reply** and **Quote** on a post.": "help:using-the-community",
 "Tap **Start a thread**, choose a category and write a title that says what it is about, for example “Level 214: is there a way past the iced gate?”.": "help:using-the-community",
 "Tell us your device, iOS version, OutBrick version, level and exactly what VoiceOver said in the [Accessibility category](/community/c/accessibility). Every report helps us find it faster.": "help:troubleshooting",
 "The bell (**Notifications**) shows replies, mentions and status changes.": "help:using-the-community",
 "The community is for people aged 16 and over. For anything private, such as a purchase, use the [contact form](/contact) instead.": "help:using-the-community",
 "The community is in English, French, German, Spanish, Japanese and Brazilian Portuguese. Lists show threads in your language and English by default; one tap shows every language. A post in another language can be translated automatically, and is clearly marked as a machine translation.": "help:using-the-community",
 "The fastest way to get a bug fixed: report it from inside the game so your details are filled in, write steps someone else can follow, and add exactly what VoiceOver or another assistive technology did.": "help:reporting-bugs",
 "The foot of the Settings Game tab with a purple Report a bug button beside a blue Community button.": "help:reporting-bugs",
 "The team needs to make the bug happen on their own device. Number your steps from opening the game:": "help:reporting-bugs",
 "The team sets a status on every bug report: **New**, **Confirmed**, **Fixed**, **Released**, **Not a bug** or **Duplicate**, sometimes with a note such as “Fixed in 5.1.1”. Watch the thread to get an email when it changes. For anything private, use the [contact form](/contact).": "help:reporting-bugs",
 "There is no sound or music": "help:troubleshooting",
 "To get": "help:using-the-community",
 "To post, reply, vote or react, tap **Sign in** and choose **Sign in with Apple**, **Google**, or an **email link** (we email you a one-time link; no password). After signing in you can add a **passkey** in Settings and use Face ID or Touch ID next time.": "help:using-the-community",
 "Troubleshooting common problems": "help:troubleshooting",
 "Use a piece’s **actions** (swipe up or down) to move it, which keeps your focus on the board.": "help:troubleshooting",
 "Use the **rotors** (Pieces that can match, Specials, Goals, Blockers, Gates) to jump straight to what you need, instead of swiping cell by cell.": "help:troubleshooting",
 "Use the free Hint, Rocket and UFO you get on every attempt.": "help:troubleshooting",
